{"create_document":{"desc":"Create a document and return {document_id, branch_id}, the branch_id being its default branch. It starts with one empty paragraph; fill it with insert_blocks at position end on that branch.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"icon":{"description":"Optional. An Iconify id; the sidebar uses MingCute fills, such as mingcute:file-code-fill. Defaults to mingcute:document-2-fill.","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"The display name.","type":"string"},"parent_id":{"description":"Optional. The parent document id; omit it for the organisation root.","type":"string"}},"required":["name"],"type":"object"},"name":"create_document"},"create_hook":{"desc":"Add a freshness hook to one branch of a document and return it as list_hooks would. github-tracking and url-watcher need the deployment's GitHub App and changedetection.io integrations, and are refused without them. A new hook starts at score 100.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"Optional. The id of a block on the branch to anchor the hook to; omit it for the whole document.","type":"string"},"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"settings":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"schedule":{"description":"When the reminder is due, RFC 3339.","type":"string"},"type":{"const":"scheduled-reminder"}},"required":["type","schedule"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"branch":{"description":"The branch to follow.","type":"string"},"paths":{"description":"The paths whose changes mark the document stale.","items":{"type":"string"},"minItems":1,"type":"array"},"repository":{"description":"The repository name, owned by the connected GitHub account.","type":"string"},"type":{"const":"github-tracking"}},"required":["type","repository","branch","paths"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"type":{"const":"url-watcher"},"url":{"description":"The address to watch.","type":"string"}},"required":["type","url"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"image":{"description":"The image reference to watch for new digests.","type":"string"},"type":{"const":"container-image-watcher"}},"required":["type","image"],"type":"object"}],"description":"The hook's type and its settings."}},"required":["document_id","branch_id","settings"],"type":"object"},"name":"create_hook"},"create_tag":{"desc":"Create a tag and return {tag_id}. The name has to be unused in the organisation. The tag lands last in the sidebar order; update_tag moves it and set_tag_assignment puts it on a document.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"color":{"description":"The colour.","enum":["red","orange","amber","yellow","lime","green","emerald","teal","cyan","sky","blue","indigo","violet","purple","fuchsia","pink"],"type":"string"},"name":{"description":"The display name.","type":"string"}},"required":["name","color"],"type":"object"},"name":"create_tag"},"delete_block":{"desc":"Delete one block by id, including anything nested inside it. Its comments, hooks and files go with it and cannot be restored, so use move_block when the aim is to reorder and replace_blocks when the aim is new content. Returns {deleted: id}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The id of the block to delete.","type":"string"},"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id","block_uid"],"type":"object"},"name":"delete_block"},"delete_document":{"desc":"Delete a document and every document nested under it. The whole subtree goes and cannot be restored, so check the tree with list_documents first, and use update_document when the aim is to relocate rather than remove. Returns {document_id, deleted}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"delete_document"},"delete_hook":{"desc":"Delete a hook, tearing down whatever it watches outside the document. It cannot be restored; update_hook without settings clears what it flagged instead. Returns {hook_id, deleted}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"hook_id":{"description":"The hook id, from list_hooks.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","hook_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"delete_hook"},"delete_tag":{"desc":"Delete a tag. Every document loses it, on every branch, and it cannot be restored; set_tag_assignment takes it off one document instead. Returns {tag_id, deleted}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"tag_id":{"description":"The tag id, from list_tags or a document's tags.","type":"string"}},"required":["tag_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"delete_tag"},"get_data_source_metadata":{"desc":"Describe what a data source holds: for Prometheus, each metric with its type, help and unit; for SQL, {default_schema, tables: {table: [columns]}}. Read it before writing a query, so the names in it are real ones.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_data_source_metadata"},"get_document":{"desc":"Read one document on one branch: its name, icon, parent_id and updated_at, every branch it has as {id, name, protected, default, updated_at}, the tags on the branch read, and content: its blocks as XML, one element per block with its id, in the format insert_blocks describes. Read a document this way before editing it. A protected branch refuses writes, so write to an unprotected one.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"Optional. Narrows content to this block and what it holds; an id inside a block, such as a search hit's, reads the block holding it.","type":"string"},"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_document"},"insert_blocks":{"desc":"Insert blocks into a document, written as XML, all in one call: at its start or end, or before or after the block reference_block_uid names. Every element is a new block, so leave id out; replace_blocks changes existing ones. A block not allowed where it lands is refused, naming what the place takes. Returns the written blocks as XML with their ids.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"content":{"description":"The blocks as XML, one element per block. Elements: \u003cp\u003e; \u003ch1\u003e to \u003ch3\u003e, plain text; \u003cul\u003e and \u003col start\u003e of \u003cli\u003e, and \u003ctasks\u003e of \u003ctask checked\u003e, where an entry holds its text and then any blocks nested under it; \u003cblockquote\u003e and \u003ccallout icon\u003e holding blocks; \u003cpre language\u003e with raw code, or with a title the titled code a split_doc's right side takes; \u003cmermaid\u003e with raw source; \u003chr/\u003e; \u003cimg src alt title width/\u003e; \u003cfigma src width height/\u003e; \u003cmetrics\u003e of \u003cmetric\u003e, which holds a JSON object of its attributes; \u003csplit_doc inversed\u003e holding \u003cleft\u003e, an \u003ch1\u003e then \u003cp\u003e, lists or \u003ccallout\u003e then any \u003cparams header\u003e of \u003cparam name type\u003edescription\u003c/param\u003e, and \u003cright\u003e, a titled \u003cpre\u003e, \u003cmetric\u003e or \u003cmermaid\u003e. Inline text takes \u003cb\u003e, \u003ci\u003e, \u003cu\u003e, \u003cs\u003e, \u003ccode\u003e and \u003ca href\u003e; outside \u003cpre\u003e, \u003cmermaid\u003e and \u003cmetric\u003e, whose content is raw, write \u0026 as \u0026amp; and \u003c as \u0026lt;. Mermaid ends a gantt task name or timeline period at its first colon, so write a colon inside one as #58;. A metric's attributes: dataSourceId (an id from list_data_sources), queries ([{name, query, legendFormat}], PromQL or SQL as the data source takes), refreshInterval (5s|10s|30s|1m|5m|15m|30m|1h|2h|1d), simulationPreset (cpu_usage|memory_usage|disk_usage|http_requests|http_latency|error_rate), timeRange (last_5_minutes|last_15_minutes|last_30_minutes|last_1_hour|last_3_hours|last_6_hours|last_12_hours|last_24_hours|last_2_days|last_7_days|last_30_days|last_90_days|last_6_months|last_1_year|last_2_years|last_5_years|today|yesterday|today_so_far|this_week|this_week_so_far|this_month|this_month_so_far|this_year|this_year_so_far|previous_week|previous_month|previous_year), unitType (custom|nanoseconds|microseconds|milliseconds|seconds|minutes|hours|days|bytes|kilobytes|megabytes|gigabytes|terabytes|bits|kilobits|megabits|gigabits|terabits|percent0to100|percent0to1), visualizationType (line_chart|bar_chart|gauge_chart), width (compact|standard|wide), and optionally title, unitCustom (the label when unitType is custom), decimals, thresholds ([{value, label, color}]), baseThresholdColor, axisBoundsMin, axisBoundsMax.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"position":{"description":"Where the blocks land: before or after the reference block, or at the start or end of the document.","enum":["before","after","start","end"],"type":"string"},"reference_block_uid":{"description":"The id of the block to insert beside. Required with before and after; leave it out with start and end.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id","position","content"],"type":"object"},"name":"insert_blocks"},"list_data_sources":{"desc":"List the organisation's data sources as {id, name, type, status}. type (prometheus, postgresql, mariadb or mysql) decides the query language and which tools serve it. Start here: the other data source tools take an id from this list.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"list_data_sources"},"list_documents":{"desc":"List the organisation's documents as a tree of {id, name, default_branch_id, children}. Use it to find a document by title; search_documents finds content. parent_id narrows it to that document's children.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"parent_id":{"description":"Optional. A document whose direct children to list; omit it for the whole tree.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"list_documents"},"list_hooks":{"desc":"List the freshness hooks on one branch of a document as [{id, type, block_uid, settings, score, state, status, created_at, updated_at}]. A hook watches something outside the document and lowers its score from 100 as that thing changes or a date approaches. block_uid is the block it is anchored to, or null for the whole document.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"list_hooks"},"list_prometheus_labels":{"desc":"List the label names of a Prometheus data source or, with label set, the values that label takes. matchers narrows either to the series they select. Use it to find the labels and values a query should filter on.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start, RFC 3339. Defaults to an hour before to.","type":"string"},"label":{"description":"Optional. A label, such as job, whose values to list instead of the names.","type":"string"},"matchers":{"description":"Optional. PromQL series selectors, such as [\"up\", \"{job=\\\"api\\\"}\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end, RFC 3339. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"list_prometheus_labels"},"list_prometheus_series":{"desc":"List the series that matchers select in a Prometheus data source, each as its full label set. Use it to see which label combinations a metric has before querying it.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start, RFC 3339. Defaults to an hour before to.","type":"string"},"matchers":{"description":"PromQL series selectors, such as [\"up\", \"{job=\\\"api\\\"}\"].","items":{"type":"string"},"type":"array"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end, RFC 3339. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","matchers"],"type":"object"},"name":"list_prometheus_series"},"list_tags":{"desc":"List the organisation's tags in sidebar order as [{id, name, color, hidden, documents}]. color is a palette name, or unknown for a colour outside the palette that update_tag can fix. documents are the documents whose default branch carries the tag; a tag on another branch shows only on get_document for that branch. hidden is whether the current user keeps the tag out of their sidebar, and does not stop it being assigned.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{},"type":"object"},"name":"list_tags"},"move_block":{"desc":"Move a block before or after another block of the same document. It keeps its id and nested content, and with them its comments, hooks and files, which a delete and insert would lose. The landing spot has to accept the block. Returns the moved block as XML.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The id of the block to move.","type":"string"},"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"position":{"description":"Which side of the reference block it lands on.","enum":["before","after"],"type":"string"},"reference_block_uid":{"description":"The id of the block it lands beside.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id","block_uid","position","reference_block_uid"],"type":"object"},"name":"move_block"},"query_data_source":{"desc":"Run a query over a time range: PromQL for Prometheus, read-only SQL for the others, where $__ macros such as $__timeFilter expand against the range. Without chart_type it returns the raw answer, capped at 20 series of 100 points or 200 rows. With chart_type it returns what a metric block would draw: status, series count, and each series' labels, point count and endpoints. Check a query that way before putting it in a block.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"chart_type":{"description":"Optional. The chart to check the query against; omit it for the values themselves.","enum":["line_chart","bar_chart","gauge_chart"],"type":"string"},"data_source_id":{"description":"The data source id, from list_data_sources.","type":"string"},"from":{"description":"Optional. Range start, RFC 3339. Defaults to an hour before to.","type":"string"},"query":{"description":"The PromQL or SQL to run. For a SQL chart, select a time column aliased time and one or more numeric columns.","type":"string"},"to":{"description":"Optional. Range end, RFC 3339. Defaults to now.","type":"string"}},"required":["data_source_id","query"],"type":"object"},"name":"query_data_source"},"read_tool_output":{"desc":"Retrieve the full output of an earlier tool call that was too large to keep in the conversation. Pass the path shown in the truncation notice.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"file_path":{"description":"The stored output path from the truncation notice.","type":"string"}},"required":["file_path"],"type":"object"},"name":"read_tool_output"},"replace_blocks":{"desc":"Replace one block with the blocks content holds, in the XML insert_blocks describes. To change a block, read it with get_document (block_uid narrows the read), edit the XML and send it back. Keep the id of every element that stays: it keeps its comments, hooks and files, and unchanged content stays exactly as stored. An element without an id is new; an id from outside the replaced block is refused. Returns the written blocks as XML.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"block_uid":{"description":"The id of the block being replaced.","type":"string"},"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"content":{"description":"The blocks taking its place, as XML in the format insert_blocks describes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id","block_uid","content"],"type":"object"},"name":"replace_blocks"},"search_documents":{"desc":"Full-text search for blocks whose text matches the query, across every branch of every document. Returns {documents: [{document_id, document_name, branch_id, branch_name, default, hits: [{block_uid, text}]}]}, best match first. A block a fork copied unchanged is found on every branch holding it. A hit is the innermost block holding the text; get_document with its block_uid reads the element holding it. Use list_documents to find a document by title.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"limit":{"description":"Optional. The most hits to return: 20 by default, 50 at most.","type":"integer"},"query":{"description":"The text to search for; matching is typo-tolerant.","type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"type":"object"},"name":"search_documents"},"set_tag_assignment":{"desc":"Put a tag on one branch of a document, or take it off. The document is listed under the tag in the sidebar while its default branch carries it. Setting what is already the case succeeds and changes nothing; delete_tag removes a tag everywhere. Returns {document_id, branch_id, tag_id, assigned}.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"assigned":{"description":"true puts the tag on the branch, false takes it off.","type":"boolean"},"branch_id":{"description":"The branch id, from list_documents, search_documents or get_document. A protected branch refuses writes.","type":"string"},"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"tag_id":{"description":"The tag id, from list_tags or a document's tags.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id","branch_id","tag_id","assigned"],"type":"object"},"name":"set_tag_assignment"},"update_document":{"desc":"Change a document's name, icon or parent; give only what changes, and a call changing nothing is refused. Content is untouched, and a parent that is the document itself or one of its descendants is refused. Returns {document_id} with what changed.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"icon":{"description":"Optional. An Iconify id; the sidebar uses MingCute fills, such as mingcute:rocket-fill.","type":"string"},"name":{"description":"Optional. The new display name.","type":"string"},"parent_id":{"description":"Optional. The new parent document id, or an empty string for the organisation root.","type":"string"}},"required":["document_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_document"},"update_hook":{"desc":"Reset a hook's score to 100 and its state to a fresh hook's, and return it as list_hooks would. Without settings the hook keeps them: use that once the document is brought up to date with what the hook flagged. With settings they replace the old ones; the hook keeps its type, so to change it delete the hook and create another.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"document_id":{"description":"The document id.","type":"string"},"hook_id":{"description":"The hook id, from list_hooks.","type":"string"},"settings":{"description":"Optional. New settings, shaped as create_hook's, with the hook's own type.","type":"object"}},"required":["document_id","hook_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_hook"},"update_tag":{"desc":"Rename, recolour or move a tag in the sidebar order; give only what changes, and a call changing nothing is refused. A new name has to be unused in the organisation. Returns {tag_id} with what changed. set_tag_assignment changes which documents carry it.","has_params_one_of":true,"json_schema":{"properties":{"color":{"description":"Optional. The new colour.","enum":["red","orange","amber","yellow","lime","green","emerald","teal","cyan","sky","blue","indigo","violet","purple","fuchsia","pink"],"type":"string"},"name":{"description":"Optional. The new display name.","type":"string"},"sort_index":{"description":"Optional. The 0-based position in list_tags order; 0 is first.","type":"integer"},"tag_id":{"description":"The tag id, from list_tags or a document's tags.","type":"string"}},"required":["tag_id"],"type":"object"},"name":"update_tag"}}